Error [jet.ModuleValueNotBuilt]: `TOTAL` can't be computed while building: it reaches the outside world (IO)
  --> tests/ui/module_value_calls_code_that_reaches_the_outside_world.jet:8:8
    |
  8 | TOTAL: greet() + 1
    |        ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A module-level `name: value` is computed while building and stored in the program, the same value on every tier; no code runs before `run: fn`, so a value that stops, reaches the outside world, or can't run while building is a build error
 Fix: Compute it in `run` and pass it on; or make it a function, marked `#Memo` when it is pure so the first result is kept; or, for outside data, read a pinned build input such as `comptime { embed_file("config.txt") }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0643
